## 15. UX and Visual Design Direction

### 15.1 Overall style

- Modern scientific SaaS interface.
- Clean, minimal, professional, and trustworthy.
- White or very light gray page backgrounds.
- Deep navy for headings and key text.
- Blue or cyan for primary actions and selected navigation.
- Green for successful upload/validation.
- Amber for warnings.
- Red for errors.
- Soft borders, subtle shadows, medium corner radius, and generous whitespace.
- Use a subtle molecule / connected-node illustration in the hero only. Do not overcrowd the interface with scientific decoration.

### 15.2 Typography and components

- Use a clear sans-serif font.
- Establish a consistent hierarchy for page title, section heading, body text, and helper labels.
- Use accessible contrast and visible focus states.
- Buttons must have clear labels and interactive states.
- Tables should be readable, horizontally scrollable on narrow screens, and have sticky headers only if useful.

### 15.3 Responsive behavior

- Desktop: centered content container, two-column upload layout where useful, summary cards in a grid, full-width preview table.
- Mobile: single-column layout, full-width upload area and buttons, horizontally scrollable data table, no clipped navigation or content.

