## 21. Instructions for the AI Website Builder

Build the application described in this PRD. Treat this document as the source of truth.

1. Create a working Next.js + TypeScript frontend in `/frontend` and a Python FastAPI backend in `/backend`.
2. Implement the real CSV upload connection from the frontend to the Railway-compatible API. Do not make the upload interaction a visual-only mockup.
3. Use Pandas in the backend to read and inspect the actual uploaded CSV.
4. Return the actual backend summary and preview to the frontend.
5. Keep the CSV schema generic. Do not require SMILES or molecular descriptor fields in this version.
6. Do not implement authentication, payments, credits, QSAR inference, or fake analysis results.
7. Use the accompanying images only as visual guidance. Follow the written PRD whenever an image label conflicts with the scope.
8. Include `.env.example`, a useful `README.md`, error handling, and basic tests.
